# NOTE: site/research/ is deliberately NOT ignored. #3507 ignored it as "a runtime
# plane like site/live/", but the estate is 87 TRACKED files (#3501/#3512) that reach
# the edge by being committed. Ignoring a tracked tree is the worst of both: `git add
# site/` still stages edits to existing pages and silently skips every NEW report page,
# freezing the estate while research-ingest keeps growing catalog.json. If this ever
# does need ignoring, render.yml must force-add it (as it does site/stockbrief).
# Polygon hourly bars for the 4H chart timeframe — regenerable + daily-changing, so
# cached cross-job in CI (actions/cache) rather than committed; site/intraday is the
# force-tracked, shipped artifact.
data/intraday/
# D14 press staging (scripts/run_press.py --staging) — per-run drafts + validator
# reports. Run artifacts, not repo content: press-publish.yml uploads them as a
# workflow artifact and --emit consumes them, and its commit step never stages
# this path. Committing them would put unpublished LLM drafts on main. The
# LEDGER (data/press/published.jsonl) is the opposite — append-only, committed,
# and the only durable record of what shipped.
data/press/staging/*.json
# Financial-news fetch cache (engine/financial_news) — transient 12h fetch cache,
# regenerated every build. NOT committed: a keyless local cache must never shadow
# CI's keyed (Polygon/Finnhub) fetch within the TTL window.
data/financial_news/
