# XG-W2 daemon spool. The fast lanes (press, earnings) now emit through the
# canonical outbox path, and they run inside scripts/marketing_fastlane_daemon.py
# on the VPS — whose checkout is refreshed by a 3-minute `git pull`. Appending to
# the TRACKED items.jsonl there would dirty the tree and conflict that pull, so
# daemon-side emissions go to this gitignored sibling instead (outbox.enqueue
# spool=True). Local guards read the UNION of both files, so the dedup and
# near-dup radars still see every emission this host made.
# LOUDNESS: this pattern is items-host-SCOPED. It must NOT swallow items.jsonl —
# verify with `git check-ignore data/marketing/outbox/items-host.jsonl` (ignored)
# vs `.../items.jsonl` (NOT ignored) after any edit here.
data/marketing/outbox/items-host.jsonl
# XG-W3 persona-memory host spool. Same posture, same reason: emission-time
# counters (phrase fatigue, open promises, relationship touches) accumulate
# intraday on whichever host emitted, and the nightly consolidator
# (engine/marketing/persona_memory.consolidate) is the SOLE advancer of the
# tracked ledgers under data/marketing/personas/ — the nightly-sole-advancer
# law, charter §2 amendment 13. Readers see the union of both trees, so a cap
# still counts today's un-consolidated posts.
# LOUDNESS: this pattern is personas_HOST-scoped. It must NOT swallow the
# tracked ledgers — verify with
#   git check-ignore data/marketing/personas_host/cici/phrases.jsonl   (ignored)
#   git check-ignore data/marketing/personas/cici/phrases.jsonl        (NOT ignored)
# after any edit here.
data/marketing/personas_host/
# XG-W6 learning host spool. Third instance of the same posture: the reply
# producer banks draft-time label observations (parent engagement, post age,
# thread saturation — readings that are UNRECOVERABLE once the thread moves on)
# at tick cadence on whichever host produced, and the nightly consolidator
# (engine/marketing/labels.consolidate) is the SOLE advancer of the tracked
# ledgers under data/marketing/learning/. Readers see the union of both trees.
# LOUDNESS: this pattern is learning_HOST-scoped. It must NOT swallow the
# tracked ledgers — verify with
#   git check-ignore data/marketing/learning_host/labels.jsonl  (ignored)
#   git check-ignore data/marketing/learning/labels.jsonl       (NOT ignored)
# after any edit here.
data/marketing/learning_host/
# D02 chart-image pipeline: chart *PNGs* are R2-DELIVERED BY DESIGN. The PNG's sole
# delivery plane is its public R2 URL (media_url on the item); the local file is a
# throwaway render input, never a delivery artifact. The recursive `git add
# data/marketing/outbox` in daily.yml + marketing-publish.yml would otherwise commit
# ~0.6–1.8 MB of binaries per night forever. So ignore ONLY the PNGs — the .svg
# chart snapshots STAY COMMITTED (the admin console previews render from SVG).
# LOUDNESS (see #3326 postmortem: a stale ignore once silently no-oped a needed
# git add): this pattern is deliberately PNG-scoped — it must NOT swallow .svg or
# the JSON queue. Verify with `git check-ignore data/marketing/outbox/media/X/Y.png`
# (ignored) vs `.../Y.svg` (NOT ignored) after any edit here.
data/marketing/outbox/media/**/*.png
# HOT-TAPE intraday renders (2026-07-30). The rule above deliberately keeps
# chart SVGs committed because the admin console previews render from them --
# and that was correct when a night produced ~29 of them. scripts/hot_tape_radar.py
# then armed the P1 radar, which renders a card for EVERY candidate it evaluates
# (before it knows whether the post will ship) on every intraday sweep: 8,068
# hottape-*.svg landed in ONE day, all of them tracked, 420 MB in the media tree.
# That is what has been printing "too many unreachable loose objects" on every
# git command here.
#
# Same argument the PNG rule already makes: the delivery plane is the public R2
# URL on the item, the local file is a throwaway render input. The admin console
# previews the NIGHTLY chart-NNN.svg snapshots, which stay committed -- this
# pattern is deliberately hottape-scoped and must NOT swallow those. Verify with
#   git check-ignore data/marketing/outbox/media/X/hottape-a-b-0000Z.svg (ignored)
#   git check-ignore data/marketing/outbox/media/X/chart-001.svg          (NOT ignored)
# after any edit here.
data/marketing/outbox/media/**/hottape-*.svg
# Publish-workflow-local fetch of the live-data branch quotes (tape gate input);
# ephemeral per-run, never committed.
data/marketing/live_quotes_snapshot.json
# D05 breaking-feed local-only poller state (seen ledger + ETag state);
# the nightly blanket "git add data/" must never stage these.
data/marketing/breaking/
# PRESS-FEEDS B1 (D05 Addendum 2) press-lane local-only poller state — provider
# cursors, conditional-GET ETags, twitterapi.io spend accounting, flagship
# counter, corroboration window, seen-ledger. The poller writes ONLY here and
# makes ZERO git writes; the nightly blanket "git add data/" must never stage it.
data/marketing/press/

# SGA (Stage Analysis v2): raw EquityDesk backfill seeds (~55MB incl. the 34MB
# earnings_calls.parquet) violate the <1MB-in-git rule — one-time competitor backfill
# kept LOCAL + archived at ~/Documents/Cluade/equitydesk_backfill/. Engines calibrate/
# regenerate from them locally; on CI/deploy they are absent and every consumer
# fails-open to the committed sub-1.3MB display JSON (data/stage_analysis/*.json).
data/stage_analysis/backfill/
# Forward ledger: nightly is the SOLE advancer (house law) — never commit from a worktree.
data/stage_analysis/forward_ledger.jsonl

# Prophet × Stage forward-shadow (live-Prophet on-Prophet accrual): the tag+grade
# ledger is a FORWARD LEDGER — nightly is the SOLE grade advancer (house law), never
# commit from a worktree. summary.json is a small display artifact and IS committed.
data/prophet_stage_shadow/ledger.jsonl

# Mastermind AI response log — ingested corpus of every user-facing answer (Macro
# brain + Terminal copilot) + the operator's eval sidecar. Holds USER QUESTIONS AND
# ANSWERS: admin-local ONLY, never committed. The admin panel ingests it from R2 (the
# data plane) on demand via admin/mastermind_logs.refresh(); nothing in git reads it.
data/mastermind/response_log.jsonl
data/mastermind/response_eval.jsonl
# Weekly answer-quality eval summary (scripts/run_brain_eval.py, W2 harness). Derived
# from the corpus above, so it inherits the same rule — and it carries LLM-judge scores,
# which are INTERNAL QA TELEMETRY ONLY and must never reach a public artifact or a
# committed file the site could read. The archive copy lives on R2 under
# mastermind_response_evals/summary/<ISO-year>-W<week>.json (private data plane).
data/mastermind/eval_summary_latest.json
data/mastermind/*.json.tmp

# Agent worktree roots. Parallel Claude/Codex sessions create linked git worktrees
# under these paths; they are checkouts, never content, and must never be committed.
# `.claude/worktrees/` has historically been excluded per-clone via .git/info/exclude,
# which every fresh clone and every new session has to rediscover — and the codex root
# had no rule at all, so it surfaced as an untracked directory in every session's
# `git status` and tripped the ship-loop guard on work belonging to another session.
.claude/worktrees/
.codex-worktrees/
